          {
            "params": {
              "media": {
                "disableImageZooming": false
              },
              "answers": [
                {
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  },
                  "text": "<div>They should only be used when nothing else works or as a bowel preparation prior to surgery or endoscopy</div>\n"
                },
                {
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  },
                  "text": "<div>They often result in a strong rebound constipation</div>\n"
                },
                {
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  },
                  "text": "<div>When used over a long time, the smooth muscles adapt to the level of stimulation&nbsp;</div>\n"
                },
                {
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  },
                  "text": "<div>They can result in electrolyte abnormalities&nbsp;</div>\n"
                },
                {
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>NO, unfortunately, if the stimulant laxatives are used for long periods of time, permant colon damage is likely. Recommend increasing fluids and fibre BEFORE this damage occurs is the safest advice.&nbsp;</div>\n",
                    "tip": "",
                    "notChosenFeedback": "<div>You were correct in NOT choosing this one. Unfortunately, if the stimulant laxatives are used for long periods of time, permant colon damage is likely. Recommend increasing fluids and fibre BEFORE this damage occurs is the safest advice.</div>\n"
                  },
                  "text": "<div>If used over a long period of time (several years) normal bowel habits can be re-established by increasing fluid and fibre intake</div>\n"
                }
